# Faker Data Generation Best Practices

## Data Volume and Performance
- MUST generate data in batches to avoid memory issues with large datasets
- Batch sizes MUST be configurable and appropriate for target data volumes
- MUST implement progress tracking for long-running generation processes
- MUST use Faker's built-in performance optimizations (e.g., caching providers)

## Data Quality and Realism
- MUST introduce realistic data skew (e.g., Pareto distribution for popular products)
- MUST ensure referential integrity between related entities (customers, orders, products)
- MUST generate data with realistic temporal patterns (seasonality, business hours)
- MUST avoid generating obviously fake or unrealistic data patterns
- MUST implement data validation checks during generation

## Faker Configuration
- MUST use consistent Faker locales for realistic regional data
- MUST seed Faker for reproducible test data when needed
- MUST customize Faker providers for domain-specific data (e.g., product categories)
- MUST validate generated data against business rules and constraints

## File Output Standards
- MUST support multiple output formats (CSV, JSON, Parquet)
- MUST implement proper file compression for large datasets
- MUST include appropriate headers and metadata in output files
- MUST handle file I/O errors gracefully with retry mechanisms
- MUST implement atomic file writes to prevent corruption

## Error Handling and Logging
- MUST implement comprehensive error handling for data generation failures
- MUST log generation progress and any data quality issues
- MUST provide clear error messages for validation failures
- MUST implement graceful degradation for non-critical failures

## Configuration Management
- MUST externalize configuration (batch sizes, data volumes, output paths)
- MUST support environment-specific configurations
- MUST validate configuration parameters before generation
- MUST provide sensible defaults for all configurable parameters

## Testing and Validation
- MUST include unit tests for data generation logic
- MUST validate output data against schema definitions
- MUST implement data quality metrics and reporting
- MUST support data generation in test environments with smaller datasets